The K2O(l) row is explicitly marked in PROVENANCE.yaml as a secondary,
unverified transcription from the VapoRock condensate CSV pending comparison
with the LH84 primary coefficient table.

The NIST-JANAF source records used to fit the packaged gas rows, including
Mn(g), Ni(g) and Co(g), and the
TiO2(l), Cr2O3(l), V2O3(l) and NbO2(l) condensate rows are retained under
data-src/janaf/ in source distributions and are not runtime package data.

The P2O5(l) parent uses the assessed reaction function from Jung, I.-H. and
Hudon, P. (2012), “Thermodynamic Assessment of P2O5,” Journal of the American
Ceramic Society 95(11), 3665-3672, doi:10.1111/j.1551-2916.2012.05382.x.
JANAF P-011 supplies PS(g); NASA Glenn TP-2002-211556 supplies a P4O10(l)
function used for the phase-normalization comparison.

Users of a datapack should cite the underlying source in addition to this
software.
